'''Sullustans''' were a [[species]] of [[humanoid]]s that hailed from the [[planet]] of [[Sullust]], and were experts at manufacturing, scientific and technological development, and economics, having founded the prosperous [[SoroSuub Corporation]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:DroidSpecialist-FO.png|thumb|left|220px|A Sullustan [[droid]] [[Engineer|specialist]]]]
[[Humanoid]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Sullust]], the Sullustans were distinguished by the two flaps of jowls around their cheeks,<ref name="Databank" /> and large, mouse-like [[eye]]s<ref name="ROTJ" /><ref name="Nien Databank">{{Databank|nien-nunb|Nien Nunb}}</ref> that were typically [[Color|dark]] and gleaming. They also had large ears.<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> The [[species]] wore native headgear to cover their wide heads; at least one of these was modified for use as a [[flight helmet]] by the famous Sullustan [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]] and [[Resistance]] [[pilot]] [[Nien Nunb]].<ref name="TFA VD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> The Sullustan language of [[Sullustese]]<ref name="Moving Target" /> was a rapid chatter spoken in liquid tones.<ref name="Nien Databank" /><ref name="USW" />

==Society and culture==
Sullustans were a sophisticated species and lived in subterranean [[City|cities]] surrounded by [[Magma|lava]].<ref name="VE" />

==History==
[[File:NienNumb-HeroesResistance.png|250px|thumb|right|Nien Nunb was a Sullustan pilot of the Rebellion and Resistance.]]
During the era of the [[Galactic Civil War]] against the [[Galactic Empire]], many Sullustans served as pilots for the Alliance to Restore the Republic, including Nien Nunb,<ref name="USW" /> a former arms dealer and [[smuggler]].<ref name="Nien Databank" /> Many of them were recruited by the Alliance's [[61st Mobile Infantry]] when they [[Siege of Inyusu Tor|liberated]] Sullust's [[capital]], [[Pinyumb]], from Imperial rule.<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref>

The [[New Republic Era|rise]] of the [[First Order]] was a wakeup call for some Sullustans, as they were reminded of the dark times under the Imperial occupation of their world. [[Sullustan splinter groups|Splinter groups]] armed with stolen technology left Sullust to join the Resistance.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

==Sullustans in the galaxy==
The Sullustan [[Piralli]] was a regular at the [[Enlightenment]] bar on [[Jedha]] and had a stool that he always sat on.<ref name="No Such Thing">{{InsiderCite|issue1=217|issue2=218|Tales of Enlightenment: No Such Thing as a Bad Customer}}</ref> [[Nien Nunb]] was a Sullustan [[smuggler]] who fought for the Rebel Alliance and later the Resistance.<ref name="Nien Databank">{{Databank|nien-nunb|Nien Nunb}}</ref>

